    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="1">
        <head>App AGu 1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="App AGu 1" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.8"/><pb n="394" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis rectum sibi petat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.9"/> fieri (fieri postulet) aliquibus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.10"/> coram scyre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.11"/> hominibus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.dagger"/> uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.12"/> aliis iudicibus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.dagger"/> et impetrare non possit, et uadium (recti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.13"/>) ei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.14"/> pernegetur, emendetur XXX sol., et infra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.15"/> VII noctes faciat ei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.16"/> rectum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.9"/> (ius publicum).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="394" ed="#liebermann"/><hi rend="italic">App. AGu</hi>. 1. Wenn einer vor irgend welchen Amtleuten oder anderen Richtern fordert, dass ihm [sein] Recht geschehe und [es] nicht erlangen kann, indem ihm Pfandversprechen (der Urtheilserfüllung <hi rend="italic">Quadr.-Ausg. II</hi>) verweigert wird, so büsse [Verklagter] 30 Schill. und erfülle ihm binnen 7 Tagen das(Volks- <hi rend="italic">Qu. II</hi>)recht.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman"><hi rend="italic">App. AGu</hi>. 1. If someone demands before any officials or other judges that [his] right be done to him and cannot obtain [it], in that a promise of pledge (for fulfilment of the judgement <hi rend="italic">Quadr.-Ausg. II</hi>) is refused him, let [the accused] pay 30 shill. compensation and fulfil for him within 7 days the (public <hi rend="italic">Qu. II</hi>) law.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann"/>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Ine 8</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="380"><label>modifies</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_8">Ine 8</ref> <quote>There may thus be no significance in the plural 'shiremen or other judges' replacing Ine's singular [n. App. AGu 1, Ine 8]</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text and German translation transcribed from Gesetze I p. 394 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page); Liebermann prints in smaller type: Wenn einer vor irgend welchen Amt | oder anderen Richter | fordert, | ihm [sein] Recht | und [es] nicht erlangen kann, indem ihm Pfandversprechen | verweigert | so büsse [Verklagter] 30 Schill. und erfülle | binnen 7 Tagen das | recht.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.dagger" n="†" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">394</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">scírmen . . . deman <hi rend="italic">las wohl Vorlage, also vielleicht wie Ine Singular.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">scírmen . . . deman was probably the reading of the original, which was thus perhaps singular, as in Ine.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">394</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">I <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">I added by Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">394</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor der Klammer Lond, eingeklammertes übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the text before the brackets Lond; the bracketed text the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">394</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> c. a. <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; c. a. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">394</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">schire <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">schire Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">394</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">394</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">394</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> p. ei, XXX s. emendet <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; p. ei, XXX s. emendet the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">394</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">intra <hi rend="italic">TMHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">intra TMHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">394</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="App-AGu_1.lnote.de.1__2" n="1. 2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">233</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Sachliche Anmerkungen <hi rend="italic">s</hi>. zu den am Rande vermerkten Quellen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">For notes on the subject matter <hi rend="italic">see</hi> those on the sources noted in the margin</seg></note>
      </div>
